  "id": "COMPOUND:17374 - PROTEIN:5150",
  "verbalization": "Mollicellin N is implicated in the pathogenesis of NCI-H748 through a multi-step mechanism involving the P2X purinoceptor family. The compound acts as a target for [(1R)-1-[(5Z)-4-Bromo-5-(Bromomethylidene)-2-Oxofuran-3-Yl]Butyl] Acetate, a known inhibitor of P2X receptors, which are ionotropic receptors that mediate extracellular signaling through adenosine triphosphate (ATP). This pathway is consistent across multiple paths, with Mollicellin N directly targeting P2X purinoceptors 1 and 7, both of which are functionally relevant in cellular signaling and may contribute to disease progression in NCI-H748. The shared target of the inhibitor and the downstream effect on NCI-H748 suggests a potential role in modulating cellular processes that are dysregulated in this model. The evidence supports a mechanistic link between Mollicellin N and NCI-H748, particularly through the inhibition of P2X receptors, which may underlie the compound's therapeutic potential.",
